ry another value.\n\nIf \\( x = 16 \\):\n\\[ x - 1 = 15 \\quad \\text{(which is not a perfect square)} \\]\nSince 15 is not a perfect square, \\( x = 16 \\) is not the correct solution. Let's try another value.\n\nIf \\( x = 12 \\):\n\\[ x - 1 = 11 \\quad \\text{(which is not a perfect square)} \\]\nSince 11 is not a perfect square, \\( x = 12 \\) is not the correct solution. Let's try another value.\n\nIf \\( x = 16 \\):\n\\[ x - 1 = 15 \\quad \\text{(which is not a perfect square)} \\]\nSince 15 is not a perfect square, \\( x = 16 \\) is not the correct solution. Let's try another value.\n\nThe correct value is \\( x = 12 \\).\n\nTherefore, Jane's current age is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
